Common Linux Commands

Commands   | Details
ls         | list contents
pwd 	     | print working directory
cd 	       | change directory
mkdir      | make directory
rmdir 	   | remove directory
rm 	       | delete file
touch      | create file
cp         | copy files to another path/directory
mv         | move files to another path/directory
cat        | print out contents of a file
grep       | search specific files with a keyword
sudo       |admin command for non-root user
whoami     | current logged in user
chmod      | change permissions for files
nano       | text editor in linux
df         | check linux disk usage
ping       | pings addresses
traceroute | lists the routers and hops it took
ifconfig   | lists your ip address
nslookup 	 | looks up the IP address for website
crontab -e | editor for job scheduling
tar 	     | Untar/unzip files usually with -xvf
ip -a      | check ip address
ifconfig   | check ip address
route      | routing table


